1-5703-6539","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Huseyin Tayyer","family":"Canseven","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Lappeenranta-Lahti University of Technology (LUT University)","place":["Lappeenranta, Finland"],"department":["Department of Electrical Engineering"]}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/access.2026.3717458","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"container-title":["IEEE Access"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/norcas58970.2023.10305463","title":["Preliminary Performance and Memory Access Scalability Study of Thick Control Flow Processors"],"author":[{"given":"Martti","family":"Forsell","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"VTT,Digital Technologies"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Jussi","family":"Roivainen","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"VTT,Digital Technologies"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Ville","family":"Lepp\u00e4nen","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"University of Turku,Department of Computing"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Jesper Larsson","family":"Tr\u00e4ff","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Vienna University of Technology,Faculty of Informatics"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/norcas58970.2023.10305463","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2023,10,31]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2023,10,31]]},"container-title":["2023 IEEE Nordic Circuits and Systems Conference (NorCAS)"]},{"DOI":"10.64631\/taxq7736","title":["Collaborative Agent Reasoning Engineering (CARE): A Structured Three-Party Design Methodology for Systematically Engineering AI Agents with SMEs, Developers, and Helper Agents"],"author":[{"given":"Rahul","family":"Ramachandran","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Nidhi","family":"Jha","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Muthukumaran","family":"Ramasubramanian","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.64631\/taxq7736","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2026,1,1]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026,1,1]]}},{"DOI":"10.2139\/ssrn.4585295","title":["Fostering Financial Inclusion and Education Access in the Global South: Collaborative Stratagem"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-9557-8101","authenticated-orcid":true,"given":"Joseph","family":"Owuondo","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.2139\/ssrn.4585295","issued":{"date-parts":[[2023]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>This investigation delves into the intricate challenges surrounding financial inclusion and convenient access to high-quality education within the Global South, encompassing regions such as Latin America, Asia, Africa, and Oceania. The study underscores the pressing imperative for concerted action to ameliorate the dire state of the education system. A considerable segment of the populace grapples with limited access to superior education due to financial constraints, inadequately trained educators, substandard learning environments, and the exclusion of children with varying abilities. These barriers impede not only individual advancement but also stymie collective socio-economic progress, perpetuating disparities in society.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The study accentuates the pivotal role played by partnerships, advocacy initiatives, and innovative financial paradigms in surmounting these challenges, drawing upon an extensive corpus of research and empirical data. Emphasizing the necessity of forging collaborations among commercial enterprises, non-profit entities, and educational institutions, it aims to bridge the resource and infrastructure gaps in education. Propelled by advocacy campaigns, policymakers, communities, and diverse stakeholders can be effectively convinced of the profound value of financial education and literacy.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;A significant obstruction scrutinized in this study is the financial aspect, constituting a formidable barrier to accessing high-caliber education across the Global South. Financial constraints manifest in elevated dropout rates and diminished educational attainments, exacerbating extant societal disparities. Innovative financial strategies, such as grants, scholarships, microloans, and digital payment alternatives, serve as potent instruments for bolstering the accessibility and affordability of higher education.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Concluding this study is an exhaustive compendium of recommendations to redress these pressing challenges. These recommendations encompass fortifying partnerships, advocating for enhanced financial literacy, implementing cost-effective measures, augmenting the availability of scholarships and grants, and underscoring the vital importance of international cooperation. The research underscores the criticality of funding teacher training programs and bolstering educational infrastructure as indispensable components within a holistic strategy aimed at enhancing education within the Global South.<\/jats:p>"},{"DOI":"10.1093\/oso\/9780197788332.003.0015","title":["Collective Memory as Collaborative Narration"],"author":[{"given":"Brian","family":"Schiff","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1093\/oso\/9780197788332.003.0015","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2025,11,23]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025,11,23]]},"abstract":"<jats:title>Abstract<\/jats:title>\n                  <jats:p>This chapter argues that a narrative perspective provides the conceptual tools for describing, in detail, the seams or fibers connecting persons and the social world in order to produce commonly agreed-upon understandings, shared meanings, or what the literature calls collective or social memory. Collaborative narratives, in particular, are a privileged space of innovation and negotiation that should serve as a model for thinking about shared meaning. The chapter examines a short segment from the French-language Figaro Live\u2019s Point de Vue, a channel on DirecTV created by the right-leaning newspaper Le Figaro, focusing on a discussion of the great replacement conspiracy theory. It argues that through a narrative lens, collective memory can be thought of as a joint enterprise in sense-making that is fundamentally polysemous and always in motion.<\/jats:p>","container-title":["Cognition, Culture, and Political Momentum"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/access.2023.3262116","title":["A Resource Allocation Algorithm for Collaborative Networks Using Inferred Information"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-2197-9970","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"David","family":"Garrido","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Signal Theory and Communications, Universidad Carlos III de Madrid, Legan&#x00E9;s, Spain"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-2185-7869","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Mai","family":"Zhang","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"AT&#x0026;T Labs, Bedminster, NJ, USA"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-6728-2784","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Borja","family":"Peleato","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Signal Theory and Communications, Universidad Carlos III de Madrid, Legan&#x00E9;s, Spain"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/access.2023.3262116","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2023]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2023]]},"container-title":["IEEE Access"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/access.2024.3405566","title":["Optimizing Task Offloading for Collaborative Unmanned Aerial Vehicles (UAVs) in Fog\u2013Cloud Computing Environments"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-6772-700X","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Mohammad","family":"Aldossary","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Computer Engineering and Information, College of Engineering, Prince Sattam Bin Abdulaziz University, Wadi Al-Dawasir, Saudi Arabia"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/access.2024.3405566","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2024]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2024]]},"container-title":["IEEE Access"]},{"DOI":"10.1002\/9781394446629.app1","title":["Appendix 1: Active Components of Memory Storage"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1002\/9781394446629.app1","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2026,3,26]]},"published-online":{"date-parts":[[2026,3,3]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026,3,3]]},"container-title":["Computer Memories 2"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/access.2025.3539518","title":["Multi-Robot Collaborative Exploration on Communication-Constrained Environments"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0006-6114-2610","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Guangdong","family":"Lu","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Computer Science and Technology, Zhejiang Sci-Tech University, Hangzhou, China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Hantao","family":"Ding","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Computer Science and Technology, Zhejiang Sci-Tech University, Hangzhou, China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-3719-4526","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Jian","family":"Hou","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Computer Science and Technology, Zhejiang Sci-Tech University, Hangzhou, China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-7286-5631","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Shangfei","family":"Zheng","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Computer Science and Technology, Zhejiang Sci-Tech University, Hangzhou, China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/access.2025.3539518","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2025]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025]]},"container-title":["IEEE Access"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/access.2026.3664486","title":["MDCDNet: A Frequency-Spatial Dual-Domain Collaborative Image Deraining Network"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0000-8547-4341","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Kunxuan","family":"Li","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Information Engineering, Guangdong University of Technology, Guangzhou, China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0009-5240-9418","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Xiaomin","family":"Li","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Information Engineering, Guangdong University of Technology, Guangzhou, China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Xinghui","family":"Chen","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Information Engineering, Guangdong University of Technology, Guangzhou, China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/access.2026.3664486","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"container-title":["IEEE Access"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/access.2026.3682111","title":["Experimental validation of collaborative mission planning for mine hunting using unmanned maritime systems"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-4826-9899","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Yonghoon","family":"Cho","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"5th Research and Development Institute, Agency for Defense Development, Changwon, South Korea"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Chulmin","family":"Jung","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"5th Research and Development Institute, Agency for Defense Development, Changwon, South Korea"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/access.2026.3682111","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"container-title":["IEEE Access"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/access.2024.3489714","title":["Deep Learning-Based Real-Time Engine Part Inspection With Collaborative Robot Application"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-9746-8472","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Onur","family":"Ardic","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Electrical and Electronics Engineering, Sakarya University, Sakarya, T&#x00FC;rkiye"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-1999-2797","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Gokcen","family":"Cetinel","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Electrical and Electronics Engineering, Sakarya University, Sakarya, T&#x00FC;rkiye"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/access.2024.3489714","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2024]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2024]]},"container-title":["IEEE Access"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/access.2024.3449415","title":["Enhancing AI-Human Collaborative Decision-Making in Industry 4.0 Management Practices"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-9471-7875","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Shahid","family":"Alam","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"College of Administrative and Financial Sciences, Saudi Electronic University, Riyadh, Saudi Arabia"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-5053-5028","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Mohammad Faisal","family":"Khan","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Basic Sciences, College of Science and Theoretical Studies, Saudi Electronic University, Riyadh, Saudi Arabia"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/access.2024.3449415","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2024]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2024]]},"container-title":["IEEE Access"]},{"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2025,12]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>This article investigates how the role of archival texts as agents of memory requires memory scholars to expand the concept of agency beyond human agency. Revisiting Aguilar\u2019s and Budryt\u0117\u2019s concept of human individuals as \u2018agents of memory\u2019, it draws on actor\u2013network theory, colonial archive studies and book history to track the shifting \u2018memory capital\u2019 of forgotten archival texts. Taking as its case study the jail writings created by female prisoners during the Irish Civil War, the article contends that taking into account archival texts \u2013 as well as their creators \u2013 as agents of memory can provide a richer understanding of how cultural memory is created, stored, forgotten and \u2013 sometimes \u2013 reanimated in the wake of national conflict.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1177\/17506980251335275","title":["Agents of national memory revisited: Women writing prison in the Irish Civil War"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-5555-7998","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"James","family":"Little","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"University of Cyprus, Cyprus"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"published-online":{"date-parts":[[2025,6,24]]},"container-title":["Memory Studies"],"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025,6,24]]},"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1177\/17506980251335275"},{"DOI":"10.1109\/access.2025.3626037","title":["CoMed-SAM: Collaborative Medical SAM for Multi-Modality Image Segmentation"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0008-7129-900X","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Minkyu","family":"Kim","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"1Department of Information and Telecommunication Engineering, Soongsil University, Seoul, Republic of Korea"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-6075-5590","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Kanghyun","family":"Ryu","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"2Korea Institute of Science and Technology, Seoul, Republic of Korea"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-0382-7826","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Yoseob","family":"Han","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"1Department of Information and Telecommunication Engineering, Soongsil University, Seoul, Republic of Korea"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/access.2025.3626037","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2025]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025]]},"container-title":["IEEE Access"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/access.2024.3520971","title":["Few-Shot Named Entity Recognition Based on the Collaborative Graph Attention Network"],"author":[{"given":"Haoran","family":"Niu","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Jiangsu Ocean University, Lianyungang, Jiangsu, China"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-0004-3193","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Zhaoman","family":"Zhong","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Jiangsu Ocean University, Lianyungang, Jiangsu, China"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/access.2024.3520971","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2025]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025]]},"container-title":["IEEE Access"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/access.2026.3697233","title":["Frequency\u2013Structure Collaborative Learning for Camouflaged Human Detection"],"author":[{"given":"Chen","family":"Luo","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Shandong Key Laboratory of