":false,"given":"Seong-Min","family":"Kang","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Artificial Intelligence, Chung-Ang University, Seoul, South Korea"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-9110-7414","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Yoon-Sik","family":"Cho","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Artificial Intelligence, Chung-Ang University, Seoul, South Korea"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/access.2025.3576445","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2025]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025]]},"container-title":["IEEE Access"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/access.2025.3635218","title":["TriGen: A Semantic-Feedback Collaborative LLM Test Case Generation Model"],"author":[{"given":"Peng","family":"Han","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Changchun Institute of Optics, Fine Mechanics and Physics (CIOMP), Chinese Academy of Sciences (CAS), Changchun, Jilin, China"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0003-8585-9542","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Yuan","family":"Chen","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Changchun Institute of Optics, Fine Mechanics and Physics (CIOMP), Chinese Academy of Sciences (CAS), Changchun, Jilin, China"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Junjie","family":"Wang","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Changchun Institute of Optics, Fine Mechanics and Physics (CIOMP), Chinese Academy of Sciences (CAS), Changchun, Jilin, China"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/access.2025.3635218","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2025]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025]]},"container-title":["IEEE Access"]},{"DOI":"10.21203\/rs.3.rs-7047360\/v1","title":["In-Network Memory Access: Bridging SmartNIC and Host Memory"],"author":[{"given":"Mohammed Zain","family":"Farooqi","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Masoud","family":"Hemmatpour","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Tore Heide","family":"Larsen","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.21203\/rs.3.rs-7047360\/v1","issued":{"date-parts":[[2026,2,2]]},"abstract":"<title>Abstract<\/title>\n                <p>SmartNICs have been increasingly utilized across various applications to offload specific computational tasks, thereby enhancing overall system performance. However, this offloading process introduces several communication challenges that must be addressed for effective integration. A key challenge lies in establishing efficient communication between the offloaded components and the main application running on the host. In this study, we evaluate different approaches for achieving memory access between the host and SmartNIC. We analyze memory access performance on both the SmartNIC and the host to support in-network applications and guide the selection of an appropriate memory access design.<\/p>"},{"DOI":"10.1109\/access.2026.3663428","title":["Memory-Efficient Distributed Unlearning"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-0266-7792","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Natalie","family":"Lang","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Electrical and Computer Engineering (ECE), Ben-Gurion University of the Negev, Be&#x2019;er Sheva, Israel"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0001-2860-918X","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Alon","family":"Helvits","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Electrical and Computer Engineering (ECE), Ben-Gurion University of the Negev, Be&#x2019;er Sheva, Israel"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-2234-929X","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Nir","family":"Shlezinger","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Electrical and Computer Engineering (ECE), Ben-Gurion University of the Negev, Be&#x2019;er Sheva, Israel"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/access.2026.3663428","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"container-title":["IEEE Access"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/access.2023.3296143","title":["Implementing Privacy-Preserving and Collaborative Industrial Artificial Intelligence"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-3777-1346","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Ricardo Silva","family":"Peres","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"NOVA School of Science and Technology, NOVA University of Lisbon, Caparica, Portugal"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-2210-157X","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Alexandre","family":"Manta-Costa","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"NOVA School of Science and Technology, NOVA University of Lisbon, Caparica, Portugal"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-6348-1847","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Jos\u00e9","family":"Barata","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"NOVA School of Science and Technology, NOVA University of Lisbon, Caparica, Portugal"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/access.2023.3296143","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2023]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2023]]},"container-title":["IEEE Access"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/access.2023.3336685","title":["COSMOS: Coordinated Management of Cores, Memory, and Compressed Memory Swap for QoS-Aware and Efficient Workload Consolidation for Memory-Intensive Applications"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-1832-1032","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Myeonggyun","family":"Han","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Computer Science and Engineering, UNIST, Ulsan, Republic of Korea"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Eunseong","family":"Park","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Computer Science and Engineering, UNIST, Ulsan, Republic of Korea"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0000-6978-5780","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Youngsam","family":"Shin","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Samsung Advanced Institute of Technology, Suwon, Republic of Korea"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-3697-8946","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Deok-Jae","family":"Oh","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Samsung Advanced Institute of Technology, Suwon, Republic of Korea"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0002-1242-6343","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Yeongon","family":"Cho","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Samsung Advanced Institute of Technology, Suwon, Republic of Korea"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-1877-7307","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Woongki","family":"Baek","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Computer Science and Engineering and Graduate School of Artificial Intelligence, UNIST, Ulsan, Republic of Korea"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/access.2023.3336685","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2023]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2023]]},"container-title":["IEEE Access"]},{"DOI":"10.1080\/09658211.2026.2719610","title":["Collaborative object handling supports autobiographical recall in Alzheimer\u2019s disease"],"author":[{"given":"Claire","family":"Maussire","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Nantes University, University of Angers","place":["Nantes, France"]}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Mohamad","family":"El Haj","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Nantes University, University of Angers","place":["Nantes, France"]}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Etienne","family":"Emmelin","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Nantes University, University of Angers","place":["Nantes, France"]}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"J\u00e9r\u00e9my","family":"Besnard","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Nantes University, University of Angers","place":["Nantes, France"]}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1080\/09658211.2026.2719610","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2026,8,18]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026,8,18]]},"container-title":["Memory"]},{"DOI":"10.1016\/j.epsr.2023.109412","title":["A collaborative control strategy for MV-LV distribution networks considering multi-level access of flexible resources"],"author":[{"given":"Lijuan","family":"Chen","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-4020-3219","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Xinyu","family":"Feng","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Chun","family":"Wang","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Chang","family":"Zhou","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1016\/j.epsr.2023.109412","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2023,8]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2023,8]]},"container-title":["Electric Power Systems Research"]},{"DOI":"10.70062\/iccms.v3i1.264","title":["Task Shifting Strategy in Diabetes Control Policy: Empowering Health Cadres as Preventive Agents in Indonesia"],"author":[{"family":"Ahmad Kholid","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"family":"Gipta Galih Widodo","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.70062\/iccms.v3i1.264","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2026,6,30]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026,6,30]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>Diabetes Mellitus in Indonesia continues to increase with a high number of undiagnosed cases . The limited number of medical personnel encourages the implementation of the Task Shifting strategy through empowering health cadres in primary care . The research aims to review the effectiveness of Task Shifting in controlling diabetes in Indonesia, including implementation challenges and the role of digital technology . The research used the Systematic Literature Review (SLR) method according to PRISMA 2020 guidelines , literature searches were carried out on the Scopus , PubMed , Web of Science and Google Scholar databases for the period 2022\u20132026. From 385 journals , 22 studies were selected after quality assessment using JBI, CASP, and AMSTAR 2. The research results showed that Task Shifting was proven to be effective in increasing early detection , treatment adherence , and healthy living behavior through community-based education . The use of mHealth technology significantly help cadres in data reporting and patient assistance , while the local cultural approach increases community acceptance . Even though it is effective , the implementation of this strategy still faces obstacles in the form of limited resources , low digital literacy , and administrative burdens for cadres . In conclusion , empowering health cadres through Task Shifting is an effective and sustainable approach in supporting the transformation of primary health services and efforts to diabetes control in Indonesia.<\/jats:p>","container-title":["Proceeding International Collaborative Conference on Multidisciplinary Science"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/tmc.2026.3692784","title":["Cloud-Edge Collaborative Zero Trust Access Control: Architecture and Scheme Design"],"author":[{"given":"Zhuocheng","family":"Xu","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Electronic and Computer Engineering, Peking University Shenzhen Graduate School, Shenzhen, China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0001-1100-6681","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Yutong","family":"Yue","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Electronic and Computer Engineering, Peking University Shenzhen Graduate School, Shenzhen, China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-3484-1361","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Boya","family":"Di","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Electronics, Peking University, Beijing, China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-8644-8241","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Lingyang","family":"Song","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Electronic and Computer Engineering, Peking University Shenzhen Graduate School, Shenzhen, China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/tmc.2026.3692784","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"container-title":["IEEE Transactions on Mobile Computing"]},{"DOI":"10.23880\/cdoaj-16000340","title":["Physical Healing in Dermatology: A Collaborative Approach"],"author":[{"given":"Harvey","family":"EG*","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Taylor","family":"A","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.23880\/cdoaj-16000340","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2025]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>Globally, there is dramatic growth in the incidence of problematic scars. While dermatologists strive to decrease mortality from\ncancers, skin lesions, and inflammatory conditions, the resultant scars following from these treatments are rarely considered.\nIt is common for scars from treatments to cause adhesions, leading to pain, neuropathy, or psychological issues. Even when the\nscar seems minimal, any injury to the highly neurological dermal layer can cause lifelong dysfunction. Refer-ring patients for\nscar therapy is not standard practice in dermatology; however, research shows that patients prioritize aesthetically pleasing,\nnon-painful positive scars outcomes after dermatologic interventions. Patients who are at higher risk for pathological scar\nformation and pediatric clients should be prioritized for therapeutic intervention. Additionally, scar management is critical\nwhen lesions occur in the head, neck, and face due to the potential for neuropathy or poor cosmetic outcomes. Rehabilitation\ntherapies can support recovery from the physical and psychological consequences of lacerations as well as minimally invasive\nor surgical procedures. Therapists specializing in scar management can offer unique treatments to help dermatology patients\nreturn to normal function after lifesaving treatments and routine intervention causes lesions. Promoting a comprehensive\napproach for dermatological care that includes referral to rehabilitation therapy will prevent the development of aberrant\nscars after procedures, thus reducing the financial and psychological burden and improving patient satisfaction. <\/jats:p>","container-title":["Clinical Dermatology Open Access Journal"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/access.2026.3719838","title":["Deterministic Runtime Enforcement: The Execution Authority for Autonomous AI Agents"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0004-2089-7262","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Abhinandan","family":"Gill-Lakhowal","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Independent Researcher","place":["Calgary, AB, Canada"]}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/access.2026.3719838","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"container-title":["IEEE Access"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/access.2024.3525336","title":["Data Overlay Mesh in Distributed Clouds Allowing Collaborative Applications"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-8646-1569","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Milo\u0161","family":"Simi\u0107","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Computing and Control Engineering, Faculty of Technical Sciences, University of Novi Sad, Novi Sad, Serbia"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-5946-4438","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Jovana","family":"Dedei\u0107","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Fundamentals Sciences, Faculty of Technical Sciences, University of Novi Sad, Novi Sad, Serbia"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-0602-0606","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Milan","family":"Stojkov","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Computing and Control Engineering, Faculty of Technical Sciences, University of Novi Sad, Novi Sad, Serbia"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-5420-1527","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Ivan","family":"Proki\u0107","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Fundamentals Sciences, Faculty of Technical Sciences, University of Novi Sad, Novi Sad, Serbia"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/access.2024.3525336","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2025]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025]]},"container-title":["IEEE Access"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/access.2026.3710809","title":["Checkpointed DeFi Agents With On-Chain Accountability and Early Policy Enforcement"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-8122-3377","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Jonghyup","family":"Lee","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Mathematical Finance, Gachon University, Seongnam-si, South Korea"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/access.2026.3710809","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"container-title":["IEEE Access"]},{"DOI":"10.1007\/s40747-025-02051-z","title":["Collaborative LLM agents for flexible software development of intelligent industrial robot control systems"],"author":[{"given":"Kezhou","family":"Chen","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-6907-4142","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Tao","family":"Wang","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Mingzhe","family":"Ni","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Lianglun","family":"Cheng","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Zhuowei","family":"Wang","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Chong","family":"Chen","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1007\/s40747-025-02051-z","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2025,12]]},"published-online":{"date-parts":[[2025,10,24]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025,10,24]]},"container-title":["Complex &amp; Intelligent Systems"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/access.2024.3440185","title":["A Fuzzy Ranking Collaborative Multi-Tasks Data Collection Scheme in Ubiquitous Environments"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-7730-801X","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Ahmed A. A.","family":"Gad-Elrab","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Faculty of Computing and Information Technology, King Abdulaziz University, Jeddah, Saudi Arabia"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/access.2024.3440185","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2024]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2024]]},"container-title":["IEEE Access"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/access.2024.3384376","title":["Cross-Grained Neural Collaborative Filtering for Recommendation"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0007-4521-9339","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Chuntai","family":"Li","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Computer Science and Engineering, Northeastern University, Shenyang, China"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-5307-4893","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Yue","family":"Kou","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Computer Science and Engineering, Northeastern University, Shenyang, China"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Derong","family":"Shen","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Computer Science and Engineering, Northeastern University, Shenyang, China"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Tiezheng","family":"Nie","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Computer Science and Engineering, Northeastern University, Shenyang, China"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Dong","family":"Li","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"College of Information, Liaoning University, Shenyang, China"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/access.2024.3384376","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2024]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2024]]},"container-title":["IEEE Access"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/access.2023.3331317","title":["Collaborative Traffic Signal Automation Using Deep Q-Learning"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-8247-7432","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Muhammad Ahmed","family":"Hassan","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"National Center for Artificial Intelligence, University of Engineering and Technology, Lahore, Lahore, Pakistan"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-4085-7634","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Mourad","family":"Elhadef","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Computer Science and Information Technology Department, College of Engineering, Abu Dhabi University, Abu Dhabi, United Arab Emirates"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-6733-2569","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Muhammad Usman Ghani","family":"Khan","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"National Center for Artificial Intelligence, University of Engineering and Technology, Lahore, Lahore, Pakistan"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/access.2023.3331317","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2023]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2023]]},"container-title":["IEEE Access"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/access.2023.3311822","title":["A Collaborative DNN-Based Low-Latency IDPS for Mission-Critical Smart Factory Networks"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-6334-698X","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Poulmanogo","family":"Illy","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Electrical Engineering Department, &#x00C9;cole de Technologie Sup&#x00E9;rieure, Montreal, Canada"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-5025-6624","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Georges","family":"Kaddoum","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Cyber Security Systems and Applied AI Research Center, Lebanese American University, Beirut, Lebanon"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/access.2023.3311822","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2023]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2023]]},"container-title":["IEEE Access"]},{"DOI":"10.7557\/5.7159","title":["Collaborative Open Access Library Hosting in Scotland"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-2840-2207","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Rebecca","family":"Wojturska","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"id":[{"id":"https:\/\/ror.org\/01nrxwf90","id-type":"ROR","asserted-by":"publisher"}],"name":"University of Edinburgh"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.7557\/5.7159","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2023,9,14]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2023,9,14]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>Watch VIDEO.\nLibrary hosting services are growing across the UK. In 2018, the University of Edinburgh submitted a proposal to create a shared service governed by the Scottish Confederation of University &amp; Research Libraries (SCURL). The aim of the service was to equip member institutions with a hosting solution to fulfil their Open Access publishing activities, with the development time charged to the University of Edinburgh (which covers costs and is invested back into the service). The service launched with three members \u2013 Heriot Watt University, the Society of Antiquaries of Scotland and the University of Edinburgh \u2013 and four years later has grown to include ten partners, with more members interested in signing up.\nAlthough the shared service caters to members engaged in both publishing and hosting activities, we have seen a growth in library partners requesting to join so they can launch their own diamond Open Access library-based hosting initiatives. These initiatives \u2013 similar to the one at Edinburgh which is called Edinburgh Diamond \u2013 aim to support academics, staff and students in their publishing endeavours by providing a free publishing workflow system, as well as a hosting platform for journal and book content. The University of Edinburgh sets partners up with an Open Journal System (OJS) or Open Monograph Press (OMP) installation and provides full technical support as well as system training and publishing advice and guidance, which the member institution can use to mould their service. The shared service members meet three times a year to shape the service according to user needs and requirements.\nThis presentation will explain how the shared service grew, explore how and why hosting services and publishing programmes are developing within Scottish libraries, and provide conclusions and recommendations for institutions considering creating similar initiatives.\u00a0<\/jats:p>","container-title":["Septentrio Conference Series"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/access.2025.3538277","title":["Effects of Operation Prediction Sharing for Collaborative Avatar Robot"],"author":[{"given":"Hyuga","family":"Suzuki","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Electrical and Mechanical Engineering, Graduate School of Engineering, Nagoya Institute of Technology, Nagoya, Japan"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0007-8013-1439","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Hikari","family":"Yukawa","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Electrical and Mechanical Engineering, Graduate School of Engineering, Nagoya Institute of Technology, Nagoya, Japan"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-6303-5791","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Kouta","family":"Minamizawa","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Graduate School of Media Design, Keio University, Tokyo, Japan"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-7917-1379","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Yoshihiro","family":"Tanaka","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Electrical and Mechanical Engineering, Graduate School of Engineering, Nagoya Institute of Technology, Nagoya, Japan"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/access.2025.3538277","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2025]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025]]},"container-title":["IEEE Access"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/access.2025.3563407","title":["Comprehensive Review of Collaborative Data Caching in Edge Computing"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0009-3412-6190","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Abdul","family":"Tawab Akrami","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Information and Communication Technology, Manipal Academy of Higher Education, Manipal Institute of Technology, Manipal, India"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-0899-5781","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Girija","family":"Attigeri","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Information and Communication Technology, Manipal Academy of Higher Education, Manipal Institute of Technology, Manipal, India"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-3243-1310","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Manjula C.","family":"Belavagi","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Information and Communication Technology, Manipal Academy of Higher Education, Manipal Institute of Technology, Manipal, India"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/access.2025.3563407","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2025]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025]]},"container-title":["IEEE Access"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/access.2023.3250407","title":["Disaggregated Memory in the Datacenter: A Survey"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-8830-8944","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Mohammad","family":"Ewais","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"The Edward S. Rogers Sr. Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering, University of Toronto, Toronto, ON, Canada"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-0523-7117","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Paul","family":"Chow","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"The Edward S. Rogers Sr. Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering, University of Toronto, Toronto, ON, Canada"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/access.2023.3250407","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2023]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2023]]},"container-title":["IEEE Access"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/access.2024.3457902","title":["Collaborative-GAN: An Approach for Stabilizing the Training Process of Generative Adversarial Network"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-6754-7567","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Mohammed","family":"Megahed","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Faculty of Graduate Studies for Statistical Research, Cairo University, Giza, Egypt"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-6844-9451","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Ammar","family":"Mohammed","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Computer Science, College of Computer Engineering and Sciences, Prince Sattam Bin Abdulaziz University, Al-Kharj, Saudi Arabia"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/access.2024.3457902","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2024]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2024]]},"container-title":["IEEE Access"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/access.2023.3304902","title":["Mapping the Research on University-Industry Collaborative Innovation of Individuals: A Scientometric Analysis"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0003-0026-4313","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Xin","family":"Chen","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Management, Jinan University, Guangzhou, China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Guangxia","family":"Zhang","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Management, Jinan University, Guangzhou, China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/access.2023.3304902","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2023]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2023]]},"container-title":["IEEE Access"]},{"DOI":"10.1515\/9781772127867-012","title":["Contributors"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1515\/9781772127867-012","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2024,12,31]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2024,12,31]]},"container-title":["Digital Memory Agents in Canada"]},{"DOI":"10.65109\/dmra5778","title":["Memory-Based Resilient Control Against Non-cooperation in Multi-agent Flocking"],"author":[{"given":"Mingyue","family":"Zhang","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Nianyu","family":"Li","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Jialong","family":"Li","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Jiachun","family":"Liao","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Jiamou","family":"Liu","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.65109\/dmra5778","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2024,5,6]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2024,5,6]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>Inspired by natural flocking behaviors, researchers aim to develop a distributed control approach for artificial agents to mimic these behaviors. The main challenge lies in maintaining the resilience of the artificial flock, as some agents inevitably display non-cooperative behavior, thereby deviating from the flocking objective. Existing control approaches, especially those based on learning algorithm, are susceptible to forgetting issues that non-cooperative agents can exploit to disrupt the flock formation. To address this problem, this study introduces a memory-based resilient control approach that strategically analyzes historical data across three distinct time scales (long, short, and periodic). The implementation of a long short periodic-term memory (LSP) algorithm employs accumulative discounted credibility evaluated by Q-learning to recognize long-term non-cooperation, utilizes a filtering rule to establish a trusted set excluding short-term non-cooperation, and integrates fast Fourier transform to refine the trusted set against periodic inconsistency. We assess the effectiveness of this approach through extensive experiments. The results highlight the potential and advantages of using LSP in flocking, enhancing the resilience of multi-agent flocking against complex non-cooperative threats.<\/jats:p>","container-title":["International Joint Conference on Autonomous Agents and Multiagent Systems","Proceedings of the Third International Joint Conference on Autonomous Agents and Multiagent Systems - Volume 1"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/access.2026.3674148","title":["IMPACT-Agent: Intelligent Multimodal Prompt-Driven Agent for Collaborative Teaming"],"author":[{"given":"Taewan","family":"Cho","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Computing, Gachon University, Seongnam-si, Gyeonggi-do, South Korea"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Hyunwoo","family":"You","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Computing, Gachon University, Seongnam-si, Gyeonggi-do, South Korea"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-6507-3081","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Andrew Jaeyong","family":"Choi","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Computing, Gachon University, Seongnam-si, Gyeonggi-do, South Korea"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/access.2026.3674148","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"container-title":["IEEE Access"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/access.2026.3684851","title":["A Human-Centered Design Approach for Collaborative Cyber-Physical Systems"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-2435-3970","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Artem A.","family":"Nazarenko","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering (DEEC), NOVA School of Science and Technology, Center of Technology and Systems (CTS-UNINOVA), Associated Laboratory of Intelligent Systems (LASI), Lisbon, Portugal"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-0594-1961","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Luis M.","family":"Camarinha-Matos","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering (DEEC), NOVA School of Science and Technology, Center of Technology and Systems (CTS-UNINOVA), Associated Laboratory of Intelligent Systems (LASI), Lisbon, Portugal"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/access.2026.3684851","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"container-title":["IEEE Access"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/access.2023.3295500","title":["Toward Large-Scale Test for Certifying Autonomous Driving Software in Collaborative Virtual Environment"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-7892-5191","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Baekgyu","family":"Kim","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Electrical Engineering and Computer Science, DGIST, Daegu, South Korea"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Eunsuk","family":"Kang","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Computer Science, Carnegie Mellon University, Pittsburgh, PA, USA"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/access.2023.3295500","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2023]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2023]]},"container-title":["IEEE Access"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/access.2025.3549357","title":["Memcapacitive Spiking Neurons and Associative Memory Application"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-2631-3481","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"S. J.","family":"Dat Tran","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering, Santa Clara University, Santa Clara, CA, USA"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/access.2025.3549357","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2025]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025]]},"container-title":["IEEE Access"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/access.2024.3365500","title":["Natural Language-Based Human\u2013Machine Collaborative Learning Games Algorithm Based on Deep Rein-Forcement Learning"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0002-9407-415X","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Le","family":"Na","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Education, Jilin International Studies University, Jilin, Changchun, China"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/access.2024.3365500","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2024]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2024]]},"container-title":["IEEE Access"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/access.2024.3361317","title":["A Resource Aware Memory Requirement Calculation Model for Memory Constrained Context-Aware Systems"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0008-1747-9704","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Mumtaz","family":"Ali","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Computer Science, City University of Science and Information Technology, Peshawar, Pakistan"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-1745-3279","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Muhammad","family":"Arshad","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Computer Science, City University of Science and Information Technology, Peshawar, Pakistan"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Ijaz","family":"Uddin","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Computer Science, City University of Science and Information Technology, Peshawar, Pakistan"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-9691-7347","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Gauhar","family":"Ali","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"EIAS Data Science and Blockchain Laboratory, College of Computer and Information Sciences, Prince Sultan University, Riyadh, Saudi Arabia"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-6423-9809","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Muhammad","family":"Asim","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"EIAS Data Science and Blockchain Laboratory, College of Computer and Information Sciences, Prince Sultan University, Riyadh, Saudi Arabia"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-9349-1985","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Mohammed","family":"ELAffendi","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"EIAS Data Science and Blockchain Laboratory, College of Computer and Information Sciences, Prince Sultan University, Riyadh, Saudi Arabia"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/access.2024.3361317","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2024]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2024]]},"container-title":["IEEE Access"]},{"DOI":"10.1515\/9781772127867-fm","title":["Frontmatter"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1515\/9781772127867-fm","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2024,12,31]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2024,12,31]]},"container-title":["Digital Memory Agents in Canada"]},{"DOI":"10.1515\/9781772127867-toc","title":["CONTENTS"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1515\/9781772127867-toc","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2024,12,31]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2024,12,31]]},"container-title":["Digital Memory Agents in Canada"]},{"DOI":"10.2139\/ssrn.6456718","title":["Weighted Developmental Memory Architecture (WDMA): A Theoretical Framework for Cost-Aware, Self-Evolving Memory Systems in Large Language Model Agents"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-2582-4594","authenticated-orcid":true,"given":"Saurav","family":"Das","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.2139\/ssrn.6456718","issued":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>Large language model (LLM) agents increasingly operate across extended time horizons, yet their memory systems remain poorly suited to sustained, goal-directed tasks. Most existing approaches optimize for recall quality in isolation, neglecting the intertwined costs of latency, token consumption, and temporal coherence. We introduce the Weighted Developmental Memory Architecture (WDMA), a theoretical framework that models agent memory as a five-layer, salience-gated system governed by thermodynamic efficiency principles. WDMA introduces three core contributions: (1) a jolt-based encoding mechanism in which memories are formed proportional to prediction-error magnitude, with thresholds that co-evolve with domain competence; (2) a D0-D5 expansion taxonomy that classifies synthetic memory training data by semantic transformation depth, from raw replay to calibration signals; and (3) a promotion utility function U (m) that scores memory entries for layer advancement based on recency, novelty, correctness, and access cost. We further characterize three failure modes-self-confirmation loops, stale-memory contamination, and false causal attribution-and propose architectural mitigations for each. While empirical validation remains future work, WDMA provides a principled vocabulary and design space for researchers building the next generation of persistent, adaptive AI agents.<\/jats:p>"},{"DOI":"10.1109\/access.2026.3666622","title":["Adaptive Fractional Differencing for Learning-Optimal Long-Memory Preservation"],"author":[{"given":"Sarit","family":"Maitra","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Alliance School of Business, Alliance University, Bengaluru, India"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/access.2026.3666622","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"container-title":["IEEE Access"]},{"DOI":"10.1145\/3695794.3695796","title":["Pimacolaba: Collaborative Acceleration for FFT on Commercial Processing-In-Memory Architectures"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-4129-0310","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Mohamed Assem","family":"Ibrahim","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Advanced Micro Devices, Inc., Santa Clara, CA, United States"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-9552-0508","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Shaizeen","family":"Aga","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Advanced Micro Devices, Inc., Santa Clara, CA, United States"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1145\/3695794.3695796","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2024,9,30]]},"published-online":{"date-parts":[[2024,12,11]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2024,9,30]]},"container-title":["Proceedings of the International Symposium on Memory Systems"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/tifs.2024.3419716","title":["Domain-Specific Fine-Grained Access Control for Cloud-Edge Collaborative IoT"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-9590-9820","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Meiyan","family":"Xiao","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"College of Mathematics and Informatics, South China Agricultural University, Guangzhou, China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-7666-8985","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Qiong","family":"Huang","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"College of Mathematics and Informatics, South China Agricultural University, Guangzhou, China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0001-4468-6732","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Wenya","family":"Chen","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"College of Mathematics and Informatics, South China Agricultural University, Guangzhou, China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Chuan","family":"Lyu","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"College of Mathematics and Informatics, South China Agricultural University, Guangzhou, China"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-1562-5105","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Willy","family":"Susilo","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Computing and Information Technology, University of Wollongong, Wollongong, NSW, Australia"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/tifs.2024.3419716","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2024]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2024]]},"container-title":["IEEE Transactions on Information Forensics and Security"]},{"DOI":"10.1016\/j.jnca.2025.104273","title":["Fine-grained access control with decentralized delegation for collaborative healthcare systems"],"author":[{"given":"Minghui","family":"Li","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Jingfeng","family":"Xue","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-1572-068X","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Yong","family":"Wang","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Tianwei","family":"Lei","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-5596-3782","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Zixiao","family":"Kong","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1016\/j.jnca.2025.104273","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2025,10]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025,10]]},"container-title":["Journal of Network and Computer Applications"]},{"DOI":"10.2139\/ssrn.7286873","title":["Dual Memory System: A Method for Affective-Weighted Episodic\u2013Semantic Memory Consolidation for Continual Learning in Autonomous Agents"],"author":[{"given":"Aakash","family":"Khadikar","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Giridhar","family":"Urkude","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.2139\/ssrn.7286873","issued":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>Autonomous agents operating over long horizons must retain specific experiences, generalize recurring structure, and decide which memories are worth keeping, without collapsing into an undifferentiated buffer that grows without bound or loses interpretability. We present a method for building such a system, the Dual Memory System (DMS), modeled on the brain&amp;apos;s separation between a fast hippocampal episodic store and a slow neocortical semantic store, with an affective-weighting mechanism inspired by amygdala-gated consolidation. The method specifies how to encode experiences into dense embeddings and affect labels, rank them for rehearsal using an interpretable, decomposable importance function, cluster and abstract high-rehearsal memories into semantic records under an explicit faithfulness check, and decay low-importance records over time. Unlike the black-box relevance scores used in comparable agent-memory systems, every step of the DMS pipeline is logged and independently inspectable.<\/jats:p>"},{"DOI":"10.1109\/access.2025.3579344","title":["Optimizing Knowledge Transfer Graph for Deep Collaborative Learning"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-3898-7026","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Soma","family":"Minami","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Computer Science, Chubu University, Kasugai-shi, Aichi, Japan"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-0053-8890","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Naoki","family":"Okamoto","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Robotic Science and Technology, Chubu University, Kasugai-shi, Aichi, Japan"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-3851-5221","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Tsubasa","family":"Hirakawa","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Computer Science, Chubu University, Kasugai-shi, Aichi, Japan"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-2631-9856","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Takayoshi","family":"Yamashita","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Computer Science, Chubu University, Kasugai-shi, Aichi, Japan"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-7391-4725","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Hironobu","family":"Fujiyoshi","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Robotic Science and Technology, Chubu University, Kasugai-shi, Aichi, Japan"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/access.2025.3579344","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2025]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025]]},"container-title":["IEEE Access"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/access.2026.3662382","title":["Federated Learning for Beam Management in 5G and Beyond: A Collaborative AI\/ML Approach"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0006-3583-4971","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Jewoo","family":"Go","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Electronic Engineering, Sogang University, Seoul, South Korea"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-8812-9874","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Wonjin","family":"Sung","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Electronic Engineering, Sogang University, Seoul, South Korea"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/access.2026.3662382","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026]]},"container-title":["IEEE Access"]},{"DOI":"10.1109\/access.2024.3505293","title":["High-Performance NTRU Accelerator Using a Direct Memory Access Controller"],"author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0006-3026-3698","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Seon Bhin","family":"Kim","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Electronic Engineering, Hanyang University, Seoul, South Korea"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-3354-8975","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Piljoo","family":"Choi","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Division of Computer Engineering and Artificial Intelligence, Pukyong National University, Busan, South Korea"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-5614-0449","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Dong","family":"Kyue Kim","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Electronic Engineering, Hanyang University, Seoul, South Korea"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1109\/access.2024.3505293","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2025]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2025]]},"container-title":["IEEE Access"]},{"DOI":"10.66238\/fsrma51","title":["Energy-Based Stability Control for Suppressing Memory Poisoning in Multi-Agent Collaborative Systems"],"author":[{"family":"Lukas Schneider","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"family":"Anna Becker","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"family":"Felix Wagner","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.66238\/fsrma51","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2026,4,1]]},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2026,4,1]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>Memory poisoning can destabilize collaborative agent dynamics by introducing divergent update trajectories. This study models system stability using a Lyapunov-inspired energy function defined over collective memory states. An adaptive damping mechanism constrains updates that increase system energy beyond predefined bounds. The method was tested on a 150-agent cooperative optimization benchmark across 5,000 iterations. Under a 20% poisoning scenario, baseline systems exhibited energy divergence in 64.5% of runs. Energy-controlled systems reduced divergence probability to 17.8% and maintained 91.6% of nominal task efficiency. Energy-based stability control offers a control-theoretic approach to suppress contamination-induced instability.<\/jats:p>","container-title":["Fundamental Scientific Reports in Multidisciplinary Areas"]},{"DOI":"10.1136\/gutjnl-2025-basl.135","title":["P122 Collaborative working between primary and secondary care  optimising access to healthcare and minimising inequality"],"author":[{"given":"Alice","family":"Weidner","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Northumbria NHS Foundation Trust, UK"}],"